venv/
.venv
__pycache__/
.idea/
.vscode/settings.json
*.log

# Pipeline output. Regenerated from data/ in about three minutes, so there is
# no reason to store it - and archive.zip is now ~289 MB, well over GitHub's
# 100 MB per-file hard limit. Committing one would produce a push that fails
# and can only be undone by rewriting history.
extract-*.txt
*extract-*.csv
archive.zip
nsw-property-sales-data-*.zip

# Written by 3-publish.py after each successful run, and deliberately NOT
# committed. It records the row counts of whichever machine produced it, so a
# local baseline built from the full 36-year corpus would clobber the server's
# and fail the next production run for no reason. Each machine keeps its own.
validation-baseline.json

# Covers manual-download.html, generated by 1-download.py when the source is
# Cloudflare-blocked, plus any exported report.
*.html

*.xlsx

# NOTE: data/ is deliberately NOT ignored. The source archives ship with the
# repo so that anyone blocked by the Cloudflare challenge can still run the pipeline.
